@patmmccann atleast in germany the legal situation is that every cookie needs consent (regardless of the value or purpose).
Not because of GDPR but because of an EuGH judgement (case C-673/17 - Planet49)

I get that it's not reasonable to make it the default behavior but shouldn't it atleast be configurable?

@patmmccann I generally agree with you...but I wonder if we just move the code that reads and writes the consent hash until after the gdpr checks?

what if we move 
https://github.com/id5io/Prebid.js/blob/master/modules/userId/index.js#L487-L488 
```
    const storedConsentData = getStoredConsentData();
    setStoredConsentData(consentData);
```

to just after this block (instead of just before it)?
https://github.com/id5io/Prebid.js/blob/master/modules/userId/index.js#L490-L495
```
    // gdpr consent with purpose one is required, otherwise exit immediately
    let {userIdModules, hasValidated} = validateGdprEnforcement(submodules, consentData);
    if (!hasValidated && !hasGDPRConsent(consentData)) {
      utils.logWarn(`${MODULE_NAME} - gdpr permission not valid for local storage or cookies, exit module`);
      return;
    }
```
